From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] scripts/syscall.tbl: add c33_set_tls

The C33 has no thread-pointer register.  c33_set_tls stores a thread's
TLS base in the fixed slot user space reads it from (asm/tls.h), as
ARM's private set_tls call does; the C33 takes the generic numbers
otherwise.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>

diff --git a/scripts/syscall.tbl b/scripts/syscall.tbl
index 0ab5316051..072ab62b37 100644
--- a/scripts/syscall.tbl
+++ b/scripts/syscall.tbl
@@ -300,6 +300,8 @@
 
 244	nios2	cacheflush			sys_cacheflush
 
+244	c33	c33_set_tls			sys_c33_set_tls
+
 244	or1k	or1k_atomic			sys_or1k_atomic
 
 258	riscv	riscv_hwprobe			sys_riscv_hwprobe
